Third-party marks embedded in this directory
=============================================

Ruling R6 (docs/superpowers/sdd/2026-09-24-index-artwork-ratings-plex/
task-C2-brief.md; the owner's decision over the trademark concern,
2026-09-24): these logos ship embedded in the clustarr binary so the
overlay renderer (pkg/overlay) can identify a rating's source on a poster
badge, the same nominative use Kometa (https://github.com/Kometa-Team/Kometa,
MIT licensed) makes of them in defaults/overlays/images/rating/. clustarr
does not claim any right, title or interest in these marks; each is the
property of its respective owner, reproduced here only to identify the
rating source it labels, as Kometa's overlay defaults already do.

  File               Mark                        Owner
  ------------------ --------------------------- --------------------------
  imdb.png           IMDb logo                   IMDb.com, Inc. (an Amazon
                                                   company)
  tmdb.png           TMDB logo                   TMDb (The Movie Database).
                                                   This product uses the TMDB
                                                   API but is not endorsed or
                                                   certified by TMDB.
  metacritic.png     Metacritic "m" logo         Fandom, Inc. (Metacritic)
  trakt.png          Trakt logo                  Trakt.tv
  letterboxd.png     Letterboxd logo             Letterboxd Limited
  rt-critic.png      Rotten Tomatoes "RT" tomato Fandango Media, LLC
                     (critic badge)
  rt-audience.png    Rotten Tomatoes "RT" popcorn Fandango Media, LLC
                     (audience badge)

Source: each file is byte-identical to the corresponding file fetched
2026-09-24 from Kometa-Team/Kometa's defaults/overlays/images/rating/ at
master (MIT-licensed repository; the images themselves are the third-party
marks above, not Kometa's copyrighted work):

  imdb.png        <- defaults/overlays/images/rating/IMDb.png
  tmdb.png        <- defaults/overlays/images/rating/TMDb.png
  metacritic.png  <- defaults/overlays/images/rating/Metacritic.png
  trakt.png       <- defaults/overlays/images/rating/Trakt.png
  letterboxd.png  <- defaults/overlays/images/rating/Letterboxd.png
  rt-critic.png   <- defaults/overlays/images/rating/RT-Crit-Direct.png
  rt-audience.png <- defaults/overlays/images/rating/RT-Aud-Direct.png

None of these seven were drawn as a placeholder -- every source named in
task C2 (imdb, tmdb, metacritic, rottenTomatoesCritic, rottenTomatoesAudience,
trakt, letterboxd) had a plain identifying mark available at that path.
